  "provenance": "Symptom-phrase lexicon written for software testing against the SYNTHETIC danger_sign_tests vocabulary. It is NOT derived from an approved clinical protocol, contains no clinical thresholds, and must be replaced/approved by a qualified clinical reviewer before any real use. v0.2.0-draft adds draft patterns for pregnancy and newborn danger signs (headache with blurred vision, reduced baby movement, yellow skin/eyes, cord infection, very sleepy/limp, very cold body, newborn fever, leaking fluid, sudden swelling, severe belly pain in pregnancy) and Telugu / Telugu-typed-in-English variants. Written by a developer from commonly published danger-sign wording, NOT reviewed by a clinician.",
